01:15:44,177 --> 01:15:47,013

1266
01:15:48,415 --> 01:15:50,083

1267
01:15:50,116 --> 01:15:52,619
Nice work, Smoot.

1268
01:15:52,652 --> 01:15:54,154

1269
01:15:56,856 --> 01:16:00,026
Can I talk to you ?

1270
01:16:11,771 --> 01:16:14,741
I owe you an apology.

1271
01:16:18,078 --> 01:16:23,983
This is not the best place
for this, but, listen.

1272
01:16:21,181 --> 01:16:23,983

1273
01:16:24,017 --> 01:16:27,987
I'm sorry I lied to you,
but I'm not sorry I met you.

1274
01:16:28,021 --> 01:16:29,989
Not at all.

1275
01:16:30,023 --> 01:16:34,761
So, I was hoping that
you could forgive me,

1276
01:16:34,794 --> 01:16:37,731
and maybe we could start over.

1277
01:16:38,798 --> 01:16:40,734
What do you think ?

1278
01:16:46,740 --> 01:16:50,010
Uh, I don't know, you know.
I just, 

1279
01:16:50,043 --> 01:16:52,946
I just ended this relationship
with some guy named Jim...

1280
01:16:52,979 --> 01:16:56,783
because he wasn't honest
with me from the beginning.

1281
01:16:58,752 --> 01:17:02,055
I'm not really sure I'm ready to 
start a new one with whoever you are.

1282
01:17:03,323 --> 01:17:05,158
Let's go, Smoot.

1283
01:17:05,191 --> 01:17:08,094
We're gonna be filling out paperwork
for the rest of our lives.

1284
01:17:38,825 --> 01:17:42,929
<i>I know what you're thinking</i>
<i>and this time you're right</i>.

1285
01:17:42,962 --> 01:17:45,265
<i>I screwed up.</i>

1286
01:17:45,298 --> 01:17:49,235
<i>By the time I realized it,</i>
<i>he was already gone</i>,

1287
01:17:49,269 --> 01:17:54,074
<i>and now I can't find the one guy</i>
<i>I ever really cared about</i>.

1288
01:17:54,107 --> 01:17:56,042
- Mandy !
- Did you miss us ?

1289
01:17:57,811 --> 01:17:59,813
Hey, how was Palm Springs ?

1290
01:17:59,846 --> 01:18:02,182
Oh, we just had the best time 
at that Dinah Shore tourney.

1291
01:18:02,215 --> 01:18:04,017

1292
01:18:04,050 --> 01:18:06,019
Oh, you finished.

1293
01:18:07,253 --> 01:18:09,956
It's magnificent.

1294
01:18:09,989 --> 01:18:12,192
Well, at least he was
good for something.

1295
01:18:12,225 --> 01:18:13,993
Have you talked to him ?

1296
01:18:14,027 --> 01:18:18,164
No, his phone was disconnected
when he moved.

1297
01:18:18,198 --> 01:18:20,934
Not that I tried calling him 
or anything.
He moved ?

1298
01:18:20,967 --> 01:18:24,304
Yeah. It only took
two movers five hours
to pack and move everything.

1299
01:18:26,272 --> 01:18:28,541
Not that I was watching.

1300
01:18:28,575 --> 01:18:30,777
It's like he was never really there.

1301
01:18:30,810 --> 01:18:35,015
Yeah. You know, I kind of
don't want this reminder
for all of eternity.

1302
01:18:35,048 --> 01:18:36,983
I'm thinking of rubbing him out.

1303
01:18:37,017 --> 01:18:39,986
Oh, yeah, I agree.
Think you better rub him out.

1304
01:18:40,020 --> 01:18:41,187

1305
01:18:48,428 --> 01:18:50,030

1306
01:18:53,333 --> 01:18:57,237
Amanda, admit it. You're not
ready to give up on him.

1307
01:18:59,039 --> 01:19:02,008
Why does he only have one eye ?

1308
01:19:02,042 --> 01:19:04,911
That's 'cause you're looking
at the side of his face.
He's in profile.

1309
01:19:04,944 --> 01:19:07,580
Well, it makes him look like a fish.

1310
01:19:07,614 --> 01:19:09,883
I know a lot about water, you know ?

1311
01:19:09,916 --> 01:19:11,184

1312
01:19:16,156 --> 01:19:18,124
Mr. Fish Tank.

1313
01:19:32,339 --> 01:19:33,940
Jim ?

1314
01:19:53,159 --> 01:19:54,828

1315
01:19:56,963 --> 01:19:58,131
Hamlet !

1316
